# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for an SMP host build (EMU_SMP).
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp build/<tsan>/emu-host ...
#
# Each entry is a race that is meant to be there. Anything not listed is
# a defect until shown otherwise: docs/os.md has how this file was arrived
# at, and what each removed report turned out to be.

# FreeRTOS reads the idle priority's ready-list length without a lock, and
# says so: "an occasional incorrect value will not matter" (tasks.c,
# prvIdleTask / prvPassiveIdleTask). Its consequence is one extra yield.
race:prvIdleTask
race:prvPassiveIdleTask

# Guest memory. Two cores storing to shared RAM with no synchronisation of
# their own is a race in the *guest*, and the model's answer is the host's
# memory -- as the guest's atomics are the host's (g4mh_interp.c). These
# are the bus functions every guest access goes through.
race:emu_bus_read
race:emu_bus_read_slow
race:emu_bus_write
race:emu_bus_write_slow
race:emu_bus_fetch16
race:emu_bus_fetch16_slow

# BOOTCTRL asks whether each core is still held. A core it has already
# released writes its own state as it runs; only "held" matters to the
# question, and a core leaves "held" only through BOOTCTRL, under the
# system lock (g4mh_boot.c).
race:boot_write
